	"about": {
		"text": "Cheese whose curd is cut to the size of wheat grains, heated to around 50 °C and pressed, then ripened for three months to over three years, until it holds no more than 56 % water in the cheese without its fat. Emmentaler, Parmesan, Grana Padano and Pecorino are among them.",
